{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "last_updated": "2026-10-23",
  "note": "Remote-access tools: software that lets someone else see and control this computer. Identifiers come from the vendors' own installers and source code, or from public detection lists (LOLRMM, Elastic detection rules); a field left empty is one we don't know, and detection falls back to the others. Windows display names are case-insensitive regexes over the uninstall entry's DisplayName. mac_launchd entries are label prefixes. Only TeamViewer and AnyDesk keep a connection log we read, and only its dates and a count are ever used. Quick Assist is built into Windows, so it is reported only while it is running.",
